From 1e29659834142d5fdbb4753b4ba423bd63412de9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nsbradley88 <3960699+nsbradley88@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 02:28:59 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 28/46] vulkan: int8 coopmat MMQ for IQ2_S and IQ3_S (dense and
 mul_mat_id)

RDNA3/4 had int8 coopmat MMQ (cm1_int) only for Q4_0-Q6_K, IQ4 and FP4; IQ2_S / IQ3_S
experts dequantized to f16. New cm1 loaders decode one 32-value sub-block per thread
(LOAD_VEC_A 32: per-row loads stay local; 4 threads x 8 values made 14 scattered 2-byte
loads per sub-block and were load-bound, -27% from this alone), with the grids in shared
memory. IQ2_S keeps a scale per 16 values (KSCALES 2) on the 128-row tile.

GLM-5.3-Flash routed experts (288 x top 8, 4096 -> 2048), gfx1151:
  IQ2_S 512 / 1024 / 2048 rows: 21.0 / 24.5 / 33.3 -> 14.8 / 17.4 / 25.7 ms
  IQ3_S 512 / 1024 / 2048 rows: 24.1 / 27.4 / 36.4 -> 14.6 / 16.6 / 23.3 ms
(HIP MMQ: 12.1 / 16.4 / 26.2 and 10.6 / 17.9 / 22.7.) Prompt 172/159/147 ->
203/188/172 tok/s at 2K/8K/32K; KLD 0.0406 -> 0.0426 (int8 activations).
GGML_VK_MMID_TILE forces the q8_1 mul_mat_id tile for experiments.

test-backend-ops: perf cases for Q4_0 / IQ4_XS / Q4_K on the GLM expert shapes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
